d Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"no"},{"name":"Robert Ray","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10531","person_slug":"robert-ray","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Rod Kemp","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10361","person_slug":"rod-kemp","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ron Boswell","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10057","person_slug":"ron-boswell","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ross Lightfoot","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10389","person_slug":"ross-lightfoot","vote":"no"},{"name":"Russell Trood","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10640","person_slug":"russell-trood","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ruth Webber","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10662","person_slug":"ruth-webber","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sandy Macdonald","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10402","person_slug":"sandy-macdonald","vote":"no"},{"name":"Santo Santoro","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10558","person_slug":"santo-santoro","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Conroy","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10142","person_slug":"stephen-conroy","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Fielding","party":"Family First","person_id":"tvfy_10221","person_slug":"steve-fielding","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Hutchins","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10323","person_slug":"steve-hutchins","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Trish Crossin","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10161","person_slug":"trish-crossin","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Ursula Stephens","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10609","person_slug":"ursula-stephens","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Motions - Mr David Hicks - Call for independent health professional assessment","noes":33,"question":"The majority voted against a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?id=2007-03-21.121.2) introduced by Australian Democrats Senator [Natasha Stott Despoja](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Natasha_Stott_Despoja&mpc=Senate&house=senate). This means that it was unsuccessful. The motion was: _That the Senate-_ _(a) notes that:_ _(i) March 2007 marks the one year anniversary of Mr [David Hicks](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Hicks)’ [solitary confinement](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solitary_confinement),_ _(ii) in less than 7 days, Mr Hicks will be forced to front up to a [military commission](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guantanamo_military_commission) process that is a sham, and_ _(iii) the date for Mr Hicks’ [Federal Court of Australia](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_Court_of_Australia) case against the Australian Government’s inaction to protect a citizen abroad has been set for 17 May 2007;_(Read more about Mr Hicks' case in the Federal Court on ABC's PM [here](http://www.abc.net.au/pm/content/2007/s1867069.htm). ) _(b) recognises the urgency for the Government to investigate reports that Mr Hicks was sedated forcibly before being told of the sworn charges against him; and_ _(c) calls for independent health professionals to visit [Guantanamo Bay](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guantanamo_Bay_detention_camp) immediately to assess, first hand, its conditions and the health of Mr Hicks._ One senator, Nationals Senator [Barnaby Joyce](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Barnaby_Joyce&mpc=Senate&house=senate), crossed the floor to vote 'aye' in favour of the motion.(Read more about crossing the floor in our [FAQ section](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/faq.php#rebelandfree).) References","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-1288","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2007-03-21/4"}
